  "statement": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{1}x e^{x}\\,dx$.",
  "solution": "Integration by parts with $u=x,dv=e^{x}dx$: $\\int x e^{x}dx=x e^{x}-\\int e^{x}dx=x e^{x}-e^{x}$. Thus $\\int_{0}^{1}x e^{x}dx=[x e^{x}-e^{x}]_{0}^{1}=(e-e)-(0-1)=1$.",
  "hints": [
    "Use integration by parts with $u=x$.",
    "Evaluate between $0$ and $1$."
  ],
